cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "corpus_pepys: The Diary of Samuel Pepys — Interactive Semantic Knowledge Graph"
abstract: >
  corpus_pepys turns the complete diary of Samuel Pepys (1660–1669) into a
  standalone, queryable semantic knowledge graph. The 3,355 daily entries are
  parsed, NLP-enriched and topic-classified into 7,285 chunks, then indexed as
  a DiaryKG knowledge graph — 41,517 nodes, 333,679 edges — with a sqlite-vec
  vector store for sub-second natural-language retrieval. The index is baked
  into a self-contained Docker image and served through the KGRAG federated
  query layer, requiring no index build, model download or network access at
  run time.
